# Migrations, applied in this order.
#
# An explicit index rather than scanning the folder: a classpath directory
# cannot be listed portably once the app is packaged in a jar, and being able
# to read the exact running order in one place is worth more than the
# convenience of dropping a file in.
#
# Append new migrations at the end. Never edit or reorder one that has shipped -
# the runner stores a checksum and will refuse to start if an applied
# migration's contents have changed.

V1__baseline_schema.sql
V2__integrity_constraints.sql
V3__seed_reference_data.sql
V4__bootstrap.sql
V5__normalise_feature_names.sql
